    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode` \u2014 across three changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property (integer, 0\u20139, read-only) to the Owner response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 A standalone helper `CheckDigit.luhn(String)` computing the Luhn check digit over the digits in a string, matching the algorithm the test uses in `AcceptanceBase.luhn`. It's kept standalone (like the existing `CityRegion` helper) so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit mapping method, and it returns `null` for a `null` customerCode.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `checkDigit` that invokes `CheckDigit.luhn(owner.getCustomerCode())`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes \u2014 it recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit` value \u2014 and the full suite is green.",
